crate.library()

# What each layer test, a file in `tests/`, needs beyond the CLI. Each test depends only on what its
# entry lists, so changing an app reruns only the tests that run it:
#
# - `target_compatible_with`: the platforms that the file's `#![cfg]` allows, if not all of them.
# - `apps`: the apps that the test runs, compiled apps and scripts alike, by their packages' paths
#   under `apps`, like `fork` or `fileops/go`. A script's package builds a `py_binary`,
#   `js_binary` or `sh_binary`, but the test runs the script itself, `main.<ext>`, from its
#   runfiles, with Bazel's interpreter for a Python or Node app (`python` and `node` in
#   `mirrord-test-utils`), because the layer would load into the binary's launcher too. Each
#   script's package has the interpreter, `//mirrord/test-utils:python_env` or
#   `//mirrord/test-utils:node`, in its `data`.
# - `configs`: the files in `configs` that the test reads.
# - `data`: the other files that the test needs, like the interpreter of a script that the test
#   writes itself.
# - `test_threads`: how many of the test's cases run at a time, if not one.
